    "title": "Underage Alcohol Sales At 2 Long Island Gas Stations Land Employees Charges - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Jillian Pikora ,\n9 hours ago\nTwo gas station employees were arrested after allegedly selling alcohol to underage police agents during a series of inspections on Long Island, authorities announced on Wednesday, Aug. 19.\nNeval Efecik, 52, of East Patchogue, and Shannon Schnoll, 50, of Medford, were arrested during State Liquor Authority inspections in East Moriches, according to Suffolk County Police.\nSeventh Precinct Crime Section officers inspected five businesses following community complaints and found two were not compliant, police said.\nUnderage police agents were sold alcoholic beverages at both businesses during the inspections, according to the release.\nEfecik, an employee of the Wave gas station at 476 Montauk Highway, and Schnoll, an employee of the Valero gas station at 620 Montauk Highway, were each charged with Unlawfully Dealing with a Child 1st Degree, police said.\nBoth were issued Field Appearance Tickets and are scheduled for arraignment in First District Court in Central Islip at a later date.\n2",
    "summary": "Two gas station employees were arrested after allegedly selling alcohol to underage police agents during a series of inspections on Long Island, authorities announced on Wednesday, Aug. 19. Seventh Precinct Crime Section officers inspected five businesses following community complaints and found two were not compliant, police said. Underage police agents were sold alcoholic beverages at both businesses during the inspections, according to the release.",
